<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/AANDERAA_OPTODE_3930/3/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/AANDERAA_OPTODE_3930/3/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/AANDERAA_OPTODE_3930/>;
    dc:modified '2026-03-09T09:11:24'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'AANDERAA_OPTODE_3930'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Aanderaa 3930 oxygen optode'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Deprecated as it is not used on Argo Floats. A stand-alone oxygen optode with integrated temperature sensor, manufactured by Aanderaa. This instrument exploits the physio-chemical principle of dynamic fluorescence quenching to measure absolute oxygen concentration and percent saturation. Depth rating: 2000 m or 6000 m; oxygen concentration accuracy of < 8 uM or 5 %, and resolution of < 1 uM; air saturation accuracy of < 5 %, and resolution of 0.4 %; settling time (63 %): < 25 s.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:R27::AANDERAA_OPTODE_3930'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/SBE83_OPTODE/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/SBE83_OPTODE/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/SBE83_OPTODE/>;
    dc:modified '2025-11-18T12:09:41'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'SBE83_OPTODE'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Sea-Bird Scientific SBE83 oxygen optode'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An optical dissolved oxygen sensor, manufactured by Sea-Bird Scientific and designed to be integrated into a pumped CTD system.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:R27::SBE83_OPTODE'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/RBR_CTD/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/RBR_CTD/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/RBR_CTD/>;
    dc:modified '2025-10-08T10:58:28'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'RBR_CTD'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'RBR CTD'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A system comprising temperature, conductivity and pressure sensors, manufactured by RBR for moored applications. This cell was not optimized for use on profiling floats, and this was used in only one test deployment. The system supports both spot and continuous sampling modes, with sampling speeds configurable to up to 12 Hz. The depth rating for a standard profile is 2000 dbar, with energy consumption of approximately 700 J.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:R27::RBR_CTD'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/QUARTZDYNE_DSB301-10-C85/4/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/QUARTZDYNE_DSB301-10-C85/4/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/QUARTZDYNE_DSB301-10-C85/>;
    dc:modified '2025-09-02T12:51:44'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'QUARTZDYNE_DSB301-10-C85'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Quartzdyne DSB301-10-C85 pressure sensor'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Term deprecated, replaced by \'https://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/DSB301-10-C85/\'. A thickness shear mode quartz resonator pressure sensor manufactured by Quartzdyne. Pressure range: 0 dbar - 6900 dbar; field accuracy: 0.02 % Full Scale (FS) between -40 degC and 85 degC.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:R27::QUARTZDYNE_DSB301-10-C85'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/ECO_BB/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/ECO_BB/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/ECO_BB/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-28T11:45:52'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'ECO_BB'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'ECO BB scattering meter'@en ;
    skos:definition 'An optical sensor measuring scattering at a single 117 deg angle, configurable to 470 nm, 532 nm or 660 nm wavelength and depth-rated to 600 m. The scattering sensor has an in-water centroid angle of 124 deg. The instrument is part of the Environmental Characterization Optics (ECO) series tools, originally developed and manufactured at WET Labs and rebranded as a Sea-Bird Scientific product following the company\'s acquisition by Danaher in 2010.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:R27::ECO_BB'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/OCR504_ICSW/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/OCR504_ICSW/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/OCR504_ICSW/>;
    dc:modified '2025-08-28T11:45:52'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'OCR504_ICSW'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'OCR-504 multispectral radiometer (downwelling irradiance)'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Replaces deprecated term  \'http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/R27/current/SATLANTIC_OCR504_ICSW\'. A cosine-response, multispectral radiometer configured to measure downwelling irradiance in water. Number of channels: 4; bandwidth range: 400 nm to 865 nm (standard), or 305 nm, 325 nm, 340 nm, 380 nm (UV); sampling rate: 7 Hz - 24 Hz; spectral bandwidth: 10 nm or 20 nm. The instrument was originally developed and manufactured at Satlantic, and was rebranded as a Sea-Bird Scientific product following the company\'s acquisition by Danaher in 2011.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:R27::OCR504_ICSW'^^xsd:string .
