    skos:prefLabel 'OCR-507 multispectral radiometer (downwelling irradiance)'@en ;
    skos:definition 'A cosine-response, multispectral radiometer configured to measure downwelling irradiance in water. Number of channels: 7; bandwidth range: 400 nm to 865 nm (standard), or 305 nm, 325 nm, 340 nm, 380 nm (UV); sampling rate: 7 Hz – 24 Hz; spectral bandwidth: 10 nm or 20 nm. The instrument was originally developed and manufactured at Satlantic, and was rebranded as a Sea-Bird Scientific product following the company\'s acquisition by Danaher in 2011.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:R27::SATLANTIC_OCR507_ICSW'^^xsd:string .
